# barrel.mjs: export * from "./first.mjs"; export * from "./second.cjs"   first.mjs: export const level = 1   second.cjs: exports.level = "two"
# the run finds the name behind both stars, so the barrel exports nothing under it, and a read off its namespace object finds undefined: Modules::isExportAmbiguous()
# above.mjs: export * from "./barrel.mjs": its one star leads to names that show in the run
# the controls: the same name read off the object of first.mjs itself, and off still.mjs, whose one star leads to a table alone
